{"cuisine/puerto-rican-chinese-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/puerto-rican-chinese-cuisine","n":"Puerto Rican Chinese cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Latin American Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-latin-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["Puerto Rican Chinese cuisine is a popular style of food exclusive to restaurants in Puerto Rico developed by its Chinese immigrants. The food is a variation of Cantonese cuisine with some elements of Puerto Rican cuisine.  A typical dish consists of fried rice, a choice of meat, and French fries or tostones. The fried rice itself varies in every restaurant but can contain many ingredients such as ham, beef, shrimp, egg, lettuce, and onions. In 2020, there were an estimated 450 Chinese restaurants in Puerto Rico."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"puerto-rican-chinese-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Rican_Chinese_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Latin American Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-latin-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Latin American Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-latin-american-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a3/Catano%2C_Puerto_Rico_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Catano%2C_Puerto_Rico_-_panoramio.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"bjornman","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catano%2C_Puerto_Rico_-_panoramio.jpg"}},"ingredient/soy-sauce":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/soy-sauce","n":"Soy sauce","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 23 dishes across 21 cuisines","intro":[["Soy sauce (sometimes called soya sauce in British English) is a liquid condiment of Chinese origin, traditionally made from a fermented paste of soybeans, roasted grain,